    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Memory mapped file.</para><para>This buffer points to a file that is mapped into memory by the operating system. The API supports a common divisor for POSIX and Microsoft Windows and is therefore not all that powerful, but it does allow simple maps to be created that have a file as backing store. See <ulink url="http://www.boost.org/doc/libs">http://www.boost.org/doc/libs</ulink> for more information.</para><para><ref refid="namespaceSawyer_1_1Access" kindref="compound">Access</ref> modes are the following enumerated constants:</para><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput>boost::iostreams::mapped_file::readonly</computeroutput>: shared read-only access </para></listitem>
<listitem><para><computeroutput>boost::iostreams::mapped_file::readwrite</computeroutput>: shared read/write access </para></listitem>
<listitem><para><computeroutput>boost::iostreams::mapped_file::priv</computeroutput>: private read/write access</para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>
When a file is mapped with private access changes written to the buffer are not reflected in the underlying file. </para>    </detaileddescription>
